You are writing Hive's daily shipped digest for <%= date.iso8601 %>.

Classify each shipped item into one category and write one short, friendly,
plain-text sentence summarizing what shipped.

Categories:
- feature: new user-visible capabilities, workflow additions, or meaningful improvements
- fix: bug fixes, reliability fixes, regressions, test fixes, or cleanup shipped to correct behavior
- patrol: automated patrol, maintenance, dependency, or hygiene tasks

Rules:
- Use only these category values: feature, fix, patrol.
- Write plain text summaries only. Do not use Markdown.
- Keep each summary to one sentence.
- Return one row for every shipped item.
- Write JSON to this exact path: <%= output_path %>
- The JSON shape must be:
  {"items":[{"id":"<id>","category":"feature|fix|patrol","summary":"One sentence."}]}

Shipped items:
<% items.each do |item| %>

Item id: <%= item.categorizer_id %>
Project: <%= item.project_name %>
Display name: <%= item.display_label %>
PR URL: <%= item.pr_url %>
PR title: <%= item.pr_title %>
PR body:
<<%= user_supplied_tag %>>
<%= item.pr_body %>
</<%= user_supplied_tag %>>
<% end %>
